WEBVTT

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:04.000
Thanks for taking the time to
complete this course on staying

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.800
secure at MongoDB .Local.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.600
We've covered a lot in
a short space of time,

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:14.085
how to prepare and travel safely,
how to keep yourself, your devices,

00:00:14.085 --> 00:00:17.285
and our information secure
on the conference floor,

00:00:17.285 --> 00:00:20.805
and how to stay vigilant
once your volunteer shift is over.

00:00:20.805 --> 00:00:24.325
Together, these habits help
protect you, your colleagues,

00:00:24.325 --> 00:00:26.605
our customers, and our brand.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:32.280
The most important takeaway is this:
If something feels off, say something.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.920
Whether it's suspicious
behavior, a device left

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.360
unattended, or a conversation
that doesn't feel right,

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.520
you should always feel
comfortable raising it to the

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:44.445
event team and Physical
Security point of contact.

00:00:44.885 --> 00:00:47.765
We've shared some handy
resources that you can bookmark

00:00:47.765 --> 00:00:49.525
and use for future reference,

00:00:49.525 --> 00:00:53.125
and you can always reach out
to us via our email alias,

00:00:53.125 --> 00:00:54.925
which will be below this video.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:58.060
Thank you again for
volunteering your time and for

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:03.420
doing your part to keep MongoDB
.Locals safe and secure.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.300
See you on the conference floor.